French function-word evidence reduces the response to ambiguous 'de'.
The 'am' piece after 'Hu' gets a separate rule for the corpus typo 'Huamn'.
English cultural labels and cities get negative values. Smaller rules cover
English tense, degree, and common grammatical constructions, two opening
markup tags, and the final 'e' of the taxonomic family ending '-idae'.

Values are training-fitted approximations, not a complete language detector.
Everything else predicts zero; many idiosyncratic lexical responses are lost.
Only the previous token, unfinished word, and French evidence are retained,
and these reset at document boundaries.
